WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.260
I decide how I'm going to be me

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.360
on my terms without anyone's permission

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.580
Now, more than ever, you're starting  to see this

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.400
push back and people are fighting against

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.080
the typical beauty standard.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.620
Owning my bold was something that I'm really glad

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:16.800
that I chose to do.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.040
I am who I am

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.160
and I really want to own that.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.700
I'm Samantha McMeekin and I'm the deputy beauty editor at GLAMOUR UK.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.720
My name is Callie Thorpe.
I am a plus-size style blogger.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.020
My name is Chidera,

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.460
popularly known online as the Slumflower 
and creator of

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.380
#SaggyBoobsMatter

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.600
The world teaches women that
we are objects to be consumed

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.080
rather than bodies to be lived in.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.280
That's very, very evident in how

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.560
women are presented in advertising.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.120
#SaggyBoobsMatter is a hashtag I created

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.060
because I found that so many women who

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.239
had a very similar frame to me were very

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.540
unhappy with their bodies.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.800
It started from one Instagram post
where I wrote a caption

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.620
whilst wearing this really cute, yellow, deep-plunge dress

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.640
and I was like: "My body exists for me.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:06.580
"I don't have to prove my beauty to anyone.
 I didn't come here to be desired",

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.500
and I ended it with

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.420
#SaggyBoobsMatter

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.540
People came in with all the abuse and the insults.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:20.180
I deserve comfort and
I want to choose resilience.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:26.480
I don't want to have to back down and cave and let people tell me how I should be myself.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.640
Owning my bold and maintaining confidence
is an everyday struggle.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.120
Growing up, I kind of didn't feel pretty or feminine

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:42.520
because from such a young age we're taught that
we aren't good enough,

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.720
we're not small enough,
we're not pretty enough,

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:46.900
we're not this, we're not that.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.720
Using fashion, for me,
has been a way to express my boldness.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:56.200
I had a holiday booked to go to Barbados
with my boyfriend and I was really self-conscious.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.680
I felt the lowest about myself and
I had to find swimwear to wear.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.340
I was so scared but
I bought the bikini

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.580
and I wore it on holiday and I had never worn a bikini before in my life,

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:11.640
but the biggest, most scariest part of it all
was I actually shared it online.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.260
I was petrified, I was actually shaking.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.700
I remember the moment when I posted to my private Facebook;

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.740
I was like, 'Oh my god everyone's
gonna see me in my bikini,

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.440
I'm too big to be in a bikini!'

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.240
I posted it online and I had such positive feedback,

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.040
and I had these amazing messages from 
women writing to me to say

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.500
that me wearing it could
encourage them to wear it.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.220
I felt a weight lift off me because I realised that

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.780
I could love myself exactly how I was.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:42.600
When a lot of people find out what I do for a living

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.880
they think, 'Oh she's just a beauty editor,
she writes about lipstick and foundation'

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.940
but it is so much more than that.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.020
To me my job is about

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.140
shaping today's beauty perception.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:58.080
Growing up as a kid
there was a certain 'ideal' type of beauty

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.660
but today there's not one type of beauty

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:04.240
and I want people to know that
they can look however they want to look

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.820
and be however they want to be.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:11.040
I own my own bold by instilling confidence
in other women through my work.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.320
I have to be really vulnerable and
put myself out there

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:17.200
whether it's on camera or
whether it's writing an article.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.120
Social media is not only
such a big part of the media industry now

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.300
it's a part of everyone's daily lives
and I think what

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:27.160
started off as a curated version of our lives

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:30.600
is now morphing into something more real
and everyone's showing a more

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.060
real side of themselves.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.440
I'm really glad that I've been able to

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:40.100
connect with so many women
who have had the same experience as me.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.120
I'm in a position where I'm really

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:44.120
comfortable in my body and I want to

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.660
help other people reach that point.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.300
Representation really matters

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.600
and me putting myself online and
showing myself in swimwear

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:55.740
not just changed my life
but it helped me change other people's.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:01.640
I'm open to so much criticism every day
and I could get loads of negative comments

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:05.180
but as long as I get that one person saying:
'You've really helped me',

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.300
then that's when I feel empowered and
that's when I feel most bold.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.820
I want to influence people in a positive way

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:14.580
so that they leave my Instagram page
or social media page

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:15.840
feeling good about themselves.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.980
I do believe you can be feminine and bold

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.320
in the same way you can be sensitive and strong

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.140
and that's something that we should
try to celebrate more.

